            <ArticleTitle>A nonparametric test for comparing two samples where all observations are either left- or right-censored.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>323-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The situation is considered where the status of the individuals under study is assessed only once during their lifetime, and as a consequence the observed time to an event of interest is either left- or right-censored. Nonparametric estimation of the time to event distribution is reviewed and a nonparametric two-sample test is proposed. The performance of the test is illustrated by simulations and by a numerical example.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
